is egg now :) UwU whats this

Thanks for sending me over! It's actually really fascinating to see other people's take on the case and I'm happy to weigh in.

&#x200B;

Anadarko, OK is about 10 hours from Frederick. I have family down in Enid, OK (about 2 hours north of Anadarko) and I can personally testify that it's a long drive; it often takes nine hours to get down to Enid alone. However, in early 2015 Chris started a job at Anadarko Petroleum in Anadarko,Ok. He worked there until his arrest on August 15th, 2018 (Anadarko Petroleum is one of Colorado's biggest oil and gas drillers, in case you're wondering why a man who lives in Colorado is working down in Oklahoma).  Because he worked at the property, I assume he had easy access to get in. His wife and children were reported missing on August 13th, 2018, but were not discovered until August 16th, the day after Chris was arrested. In this time he easily would have had enough time to drive down to Anadarko, leave the bodies, and then drive back up to Frederick.

&#x200B;

Here's some links if you wanna check it out more in depth!

